(2400243, 329854, 30364, '<td valign="top">I didn''t know there''d been more than one.  I''m torn; it''s a technically superb photograph, it''s convincingly staged (and cleverly inverted in orientation), but for all its visual impact it still has a phony, theatrical look about it.  Of course, that doesn''t make it a bad image, in this or any other context.  Maybe it''s because this Christ looks so much like an Australian fast bowler (that''s cricket) called Jason "Dizzy" Gillespie that I just can''t take him seriously as a messiah.  It would certainly make a very effective movie poster, where its undemanding and unequivocal qualities would be an advantage.  8.</td>', 'I didn''t know there''d been more than one.  I''m torn; it''s a technically superb photograph, it''s convincingly staged (and cleverly inverted in orientation), but for all its visual impact it still has a phony, theatrical look about it.  Of course, that doesn''t make it a bad image, in this or any other context.  Maybe it''s because this Christ looks so much like an Australian fast bowler (that''s cricket) called Jason "Dizzy" Gillespie that I just can''t take him seriously as a messiah.  It would certainly make a very effective movie poster, where its undemanding and unequivocal qualities would be an advantage.  8.', '2006-05-10 07:28:12.000000', NULL, 1),
