(2400557, 331127, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is terrific.  It has great lighting and composition, and the post processing is jagged-edged (i.e. just right).  Maybe the most instructive thing is how much more convincing it is to <i>not</i> show the face, rather than to do the conventional thing and try to simulate a suitably manic and tortured facial expression.  It''s a fact well understood by exotic dancers; what you don''t reveal can be much more stimulating and memorable than what you do expose.<br/>I like this photo very much, and I''d no doubt like the movie, too.  9.</td>', 'This is terrific.  It has great lighting and composition, and the post processing is jagged-edged (i.e. just right).  Maybe the most instructive thing is how much more convincing it is to not show the face, rather than to do the conventional thing and try to simulate a suitably manic and tortured facial expression.  It''s a fact well understood by exotic dancers; what you don''t reveal can be much more stimulating and memorable than what you do expose.I like this photo very much, and I''d no doubt like the movie, too.  9.', '2006-05-10 09:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2400590, 331329, 29797, '<td valign="top">What a gorgeous... sunset! Very nice composition and lighting, with a great theme to it. I just now noticed the rifle, it seems just a tad dark on the stock IMO. Of course, I might have been distracted by the pretty... um, sunset. ;-) This will do very well, good luck!</td>', 'What a gorgeous... sunset! Very nice composition and lighting, with a great theme to it. I just now noticed the rifle, it seems just a tad dark on the stock IMO. Of course, I might have been distracted by the pretty... um, sunset. ;-) This will do very well, good luck!', '2006-05-10 09:46:35.000000', NULL, 1),
