(2419480, 330790, 42601, '<td valign="top">He he he, thanks eschelar. <br/> <br/>Dont worry, as I said above, venting''s over! :)<br/> <br/>The reason I chose this crop, was that I wanted "Diana" to appear almost withdrawn, which is how I would kind of imagine a sinister person to be. I disagree that the carrot had to take center stage, that would make it too obvious?<br/> <br/>This movie, in it''s totally ridiculous form, wouldve been about DIANA and HER POSSESSED CARROT. Thats why the carrot isnt singled out. I still believe the ''subtlety'' of the carrot in this pic makes it even more sinister in a sense. <br/> <br/>Thinking out of the box here - looking at Diana... would you take that carrot from her? To me logically - if a "possessed" object was in the hands of a madwoman (Diana), my mind automaticaaly says that the carrot makes her evil. <br/> <br/>BUT, this movie is about Diana and what she does with her possessed carrot, so no reason to single out the Carrot. Diana and the word Carrot is in the title after all, so they go hand-in-hand.<br/> <br/>He he he... anyhow, like Bear_music said to me, i''m overreacting and this is just a lesson I have to learn about how to think next time. :)<br/> <br/>Thanks for the input though eschelar, I really appreciate it!<br/></td>', 'He he he, thanks eschelar.  Dont worry, as I said above, venting''s over! :) The reason I chose this crop, was that I wanted "Diana" to appear almost withdrawn, which is how I would kind of imagine a sinister person to be. I disagree that the carrot had to take center stage, that would make it too obvious? This movie, in it''s totally ridiculous form, wouldve been about DIANA and HER POSSESSED CARROT. Thats why the carrot isnt singled out. I still believe the ''subtlety'' of the carrot in this pic makes it even more sinister in a sense.  Thinking out of the box here - looking at Diana... would you take that carrot from her? To me logically - if a "possessed" object was in the hands of a madwoman (Diana), my mind automaticaaly says that the carrot makes her evil.  BUT, this movie is about Diana and what she does with her possessed carrot, so no reason to single out the Carrot. Diana and the word Carrot is in the title after all, so they go hand-in-hand. He he he... anyhow, like Bear_music said to me, i''m overreacting and this is just a lesson I have to learn about how to think next time. :) Thanks for the input though eschelar, I really appreciate it!', '2006-05-16 02:02:14.000000', NULL, 0),
